                        "content": "First, find the Laplace transform of the trigonometric component, $\\sin(2t)$, using the standard formula $\\mathcal{L}\\{\\sin(\\omega t)\\} = \\frac{\\omega}{s^2 + \\omega^2}$: $\\mathcal{L}\\{\\sin(2t)\\} = \\frac{2}{s^2 + 2^2} = \\frac{2}{s^2 + 4}$."
