            "topic": "Gas Laws",
            "title": "Standard Temperature and Pressure",
            "question": "In chemical engineering calculations, 'Standard Temperature and Pressure' (STP) is universally defined by IUPAC as a physical temperature of $0^\\circ\\text{C}$ ($273.15\\text{ K}$) and an absolute pressure of exactly:",
