                        "title": "The Modern Standard",
                        "content": "However, IUPAC officially changed the strict definition of STP in 1982 to exactly $100\\text{ kPa}$ ($1\\text{ bar}$). Under this modern standard, $1\\text{ mole}$ of an ideal gas physically occupies exactly $22.71\\text{ Liters}$ of volume, not the traditional $22.4\\text{ Liters}$."
