            "title": "Nyquist-Shannon Sampling Theorem",
            "question": "When converting a continuous analog sensor signal (like a sound wave) into discrete digital data, the mathematical Nyquist-Shannon Sampling Theorem dictates that the computer's sampling rate must be strictly greater than:",
