                        "title": "The Power Failure",
                        "content": "If the power dies, the computer forgets the tally. If you spin the motor by hand while the power is off, the computer wakes up with zero idea where the shaft is. An 'absolute' encoder fixes this by giving every degree of the circle a unique, permanently readable optical barcode."
