            "question": "A Ground Fault Circuit Interrupter (GFCI) outlet in an industrial bathroom is designed to save a worker's life if they drop a power tool in a puddle of water. It achieves this mathematically by rapidly comparing the electrical current flowing OUT on the 'hot' wire with the current flowing BACK IN on the 'neutral' wire. If the two currents do not perfectly match, what physical assumption does the GFCI make?",
