            "question": "In a formal Failure Mode and Effects Analysis (FMEA), engineers mathematically calculate a 'Risk Priority Number' (RPN) for every single possible hazard in a machine. The RPN is calculated by multiplying three specific scored variables together. Which of the following is NOT one of those three variables?",
