            "topic": "Heat Treatment",
            "title": "Tempering",
            "question": "After quenching steel to form Martensite, the metal is often so brittle that it will shatter like glass if dropped on the floor. To make the tool actually usable, engineers perform a heat treatment called 'Tempering'. Physically, Tempering involves:",
