                        "title": "Hole Basis Rationale",
                        "content": "In a hole-basis system, the hole size is kept constant (fundamental deviation 'H', where the lower limit is equal to basic size), and the shaft size is varied to achieve the desired class of fit. This minimizes tooling costs since reamers, broaches, and plug gauges are standard, fixed sizes."
