            "title": "Jam Density",
            "question": "In the macroscopic Greenshields traffic flow model, 'Jam Density' ($k_j$) mathematically occurs strictly when the traffic flow is completely stopped in gridlock. At this exact point, the Traffic Flow ($q$) and the Speed ($u$) are mathematically equal to:",
