                        "title": "Force Method Principle",
                        "content": "The primary structure is a released (determinate) structure. The redundant R is found by requiring that the deflection at that support (due to applied loads on the primary structure plus R times the unit-load deflection) equals zero (if the original support was fixed) — this is the compatibility condition."
