            "question": "If a surveyor uses a $100\\text{-foot}$ steel tape to measure a long distance on a freezing winter day ($10^\\circ\\text{F}$), the tape will physically shrink. If the surveyor does not apply a mathematical temperature correction, the recorded distance written in their field book will be:",
