            "topic": "Global Positioning System",
            "title": "Minimum Satellites",
            "question": "To mathematically calculate a highly accurate 3-Dimensional geographic position (Latitude, Longitude, and Elevation) using the Global Positioning System (GPS), a surveying receiver must simultaneously lock onto signals from an absolute minimum of:",
