            "topic": "Coordinate Systems",
            "title": "State Plane Coordinates",
            "question": "In the United States, the State Plane Coordinate System (SPCS) divides all 50 states into mathematically flat 2D geographic zones. The geometric projections used to flatten the curved earth into these zones are primarily the Transverse Mercator cylinder and the:",
            "question_image": "",
