            "topic": "Topography",
            "title": "Interpolation",
            "question": "When a surveyor is drafting a topographic map by hand, they have shot a point at Elevation $102.0\\text{ ft}$ and another point at $108.0\\text{ ft}$ that is exactly $60\\text{ feet}$ away horizontally. Assuming a perfectly uniform slope, the $105.0\\text{ ft}$ contour line must be drawn mathematically at exactly what horizontal distance from the $102.0\\text{ ft}$ point?",
