            "topic": "Geodesy",
            "title": "Geoid vs Ellipsoid",
            "question": "In advanced GPS surveying and geodesy, elevations can be mathematically referenced to the 'Ellipsoid' or the 'Geoid'. The Geoid is a highly complex, lumpy, undulating mathematical model of the earth that perfectly represents:",
            "question_image": "",
