            "question": "The analog Convolution Integral requires calculus. In discrete digital time, the Convolution Sum ($y[n] = \\sum x[k]h[n-k]$) is just a loop of multiplication. If $x$ has exactly $10$ data points, and the filter $h$ has exactly $5$ data points, mathematically EXACTLY how many data points will the physical output $y$ contain?",
