                        "title": "The Overlap",
                        "content": "At $T=1$, the nose of the train hits the tunnel. The train slowly slides through. It isn't completely 'out' of the tunnel until the very last car of the train finally leaves the very end of the tunnel. This takes exactly $10 + 5 - 1 = 14$ total steps to completely slide past each other. If the computer array is only size $10$, it will violently chop off the 'echo tail' of the sound."
