            "title": "CPU Cache (L1/L2)",
            "question": "To mathematically defeat the massive speed penalty of the Von Neumann bottleneck, engineers build 'Cache' memory (L1, L2, L3) physically directly onto the CPU silicon. Cache mathematically relies on the 'Principle of Locality'. What does this physical principle state?",
