            "question": "A solute is diffusing from gas phase to liquid phase. The bulk gas mole fraction is $y = 0.08$ and bulk liquid mole fraction is $x = 0.01$. The local film coefficients are $k_y = 2.0\\text{ mol}/(\\text{m}^2\\cdot\\text{s})$ and $k_x = 4.0\\text{ mol}/(\\text{m}^2\\cdot\\text{s})$. The gas-liquid interface equilibrium follows $y_i = 3.0 x_i$. Calculate the interfacial liquid mole fraction ($x_i$).",
