            "title": "Adiabatic Temperature Rise",
            "question": "If an engineer runs a highly Exothermic liquid reaction in a perfectly insulated (Adiabatic) CSTR, the released heat cannot escape. The mathematical equation $\\Delta T = \\frac{-\\Delta H_{rxn} X_A}{C_p}$ calculates the exact 'Adiabatic Temperature Rise'. If the heat generation geometrically outpaces the cooling capacity, the reactor will experience a catastrophic:",
