            "question": "In biochemical engineering, the 'Michaelis-Menten' equation ($-r_s = \\frac{V_{max} [S]}{K_m + [S]}$) is used to mathematically model exactly how fast biological Enzymes break down Substrates (like breaking down sugar). A bizarre mathematical feature of this equation is that at incredibly HIGH substrate concentrations ($[S] \\gg K_m$), the reaction strictly acts like a:",
