            "title": "Rate Constant Units",
            "question": "The mathematical units for a reaction's Rate Constant ($k$) magically change depending on the Order of the reaction. If an engineer sees that $k = 0.05\\text{ s}^{-1}$ (inverse seconds), they mathematically and instantly know with absolute certainty that the reaction MUST be:",
