            "topic": "Heat Exchanger Networks",
            "title": "Pinch Technology",
            "question": "In modern chemical plant design, engineers mathematically optimize the entire factory's energy consumption using 'Pinch Analysis'. The absolute fundamental rule of Pinch Technology strictly dictates that an engineer MUST NOT:",
            "question_image": "",
            "times_presented": 0,
            "options": [
                {
                    "label": "A",
                    "text": "Use insulation on pipes",
                    "is_correct": false
                },
                {
                    "label": "B",
                    "text": "Physically transfer heat across the Pinch point, use external hot utilities (steam) BELOW the Pinch, or use external cold utilities (cooling water) ABOVE the Pinch",
                    "is_correct": true
                },
                {
                    "label": "C",
                    "text": "Use Counter-flow heat exchangers",
                    "is_correct": false
                },
                {
                    "label": "D",
                    "text": "Run the plant at steady state",
                    "is_correct": false
                }
            ],
            "solution": {
                "steps": [
                    {
                        "title": "The Pinch Point",
                        "content": "The 'Pinch' is the tightest temperature bottleneck in the entire factory. It mathematically divides the factory into a Hot Zone and a Cold Zone."
                    },
                    {
                        "title": "The Violation",
                        "content": "If you use expensive boiler steam to heat something BELOW the pinch, you are dumping heat into the Cold Zone. The Cold Zone already has too much heat. You will just be mathematically forced to buy an equally massive amount of expensive cooling-water to remove that exact same heat later. It is literally paying twice to accomplish nothing."
                    }
                ],
                "solution_image": "",
                "video_explanation": "",
                "final_answer": "B"
            },
